        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>In the math section of the SAT exam, you may be asked to identify conditions where a linear equation has zero, one, or infinitely many solutions. This concept often appears in questions such as: \u201cIf this equation has no solution, what must be true about the constants?\u201d</p>",
            "readable_text": "In the math section of the SAT exam, you may be asked to identify conditions where a linear equation has zero, one, or infinitely many solutions. This concept often appears in questions such as: \u201cIf this equation has no solution, what must be true about the constants?\u201d",
