            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We start by expanding the products on both sides of the equation and simplifying:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u2212 6(x \u2212 10)|= 2(30 \u2212 x); \u2212 6x + 60|= 60 \u2212 2x; \u2212 4x|= 0; x|= 0]</span></p><p>Therefore, this equation has <strong>exactly one</strong> solution, <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x = 0.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We start by expanding the products on both sides of the equation and simplifying:\n\n[MATH: \u2212 6(x \u2212 10)|= 2(30 \u2212 x); \u2212 6x + 60|= 60 \u2212 2x; \u2212 4x|= 0; x|= 0]\n\nTherefore, this equation has exactly one solution, [MATH: x = 0.]",
